I recommand boots of Water Walking rather than jumping or speed, because  
of the spell of create pool used by Liches (genociding L might be  
sufficient, I don't remember if other use this spell).

A reliable way to get drain resistance is good in case you encounter  
gnolls with wand of draining.

The main difference in the end game between Slash'em and Nethack is the  
guaranteed encounter with Demogorgon. This one killed me a couple of  
times... Good ways to deal with this include preparing stone grenades  
before hand or polymorphing into a basilisk when meeting him (and let him  
auto-stone while hitting you, a basilisk having more HP than a cockatrice,  
you'll probably won't die and revert to naked normal form in the middle of  
the crowd...)

You may want to wish for an amulet of unchanging (if you haven't one).  
Polymorphing into a crystal golem is fun and simple (300HP, all the  
resistances you've ever dreamed about, breath attack, can wear some armor).

Popular late wish also include figurines of Solar. 80% chance of an  
uber-pet that can wield weapons is nice.

If you haven't one, you can wish for a permanent light source (magic  
candle). Always useful.

Notice that if you want to abuse wishing, you can farm gypsies (they are  
reverse genocidable...)

But if you feel more than enough to ascend Nethack *and* have a reliable  
way to kill the big-D, you'll probably manage to ascend.

